1
00:00:08,620 --> 00:00:11,140
Brighten up the room and
step back to take a look.

2
00:00:20,260 --> 00:00:24,280
Anyone without money, come to me.

3
00:00:24,280 --> 00:00:29,000
I don't have any either, so don't worry.

4
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:32,800
Look at the blue sky,

5
00:00:33,780 --> 00:00:36,300
the white clouds.

6
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:42,820
Somehow it'll all work out in time.

7
00:00:55,920 --> 00:00:59,920
Anyone without a job, come to me.

8
00:01:00,600 --> 00:01:04,500
I don't have any either, so don't worry.

9
00:01:04,500 --> 00:01:08,560
Look, it's burning.

10
00:01:09,980 --> 00:01:11,580
Steel clouds.

11
00:01:13,040 --> 00:01:18,260
Somehow it'll all work out in time.

12
00:01:20,280 --> 00:01:21,540
You understand, right?

13
00:01:21,540 --> 00:01:23,500
Got it, got it.

14
00:01:23,500 --> 00:01:27,420
Once you understand, follow me quietly.

15
00:01:42,720 --> 00:01:44,260
Renovation plan

16
00:01:46,760 --> 00:01:48,540
The neighborhood chairman has a cold?

17
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:50,080
That's right.

18
00:01:50,080 --> 00:01:53,680
Well, he wants to come down and
consult with Ryo-san about something.

19
00:01:53,680 --> 00:01:54,540
Me?

20
00:01:54,540 --> 00:01:56,460
I wonder what it could be.

21
00:01:56,460 --> 00:01:58,720
Why don't you stop by and
check on him while you're at it?

22
00:01:59,060 --> 00:02:01,480
I guess I'll do that.

23
00:02:02,180 --> 00:02:04,140
Ow ow

24
00:02:04,140 --> 00:02:05,780
Ow ow

25
00:02:05,780 --> 00:02:08,260
Ow ow

26
00:02:08,260 --> 00:02:09,820
Here it is.

27
00:02:10,840 --> 00:02:11,760
Excuse me.

28
00:02:12,700 --> 00:02:13,620
Ryo-san!

29
00:02:14,440 --> 00:02:17,060
I heard he has a cold,
so I'll come in for a bit.

30
00:02:18,800 --> 00:02:20,740
What is it? You need me for something?

31
00:02:20,740 --> 00:02:23,100
Ryo-san, thanks for coming.

32
00:02:24,340 --> 00:02:25,920
Never mind, just lie down.

33
00:02:26,900 --> 00:02:30,420
Actually,
it's about the neighborhood festival.

34
00:02:30,420 --> 00:02:33,160
The festival? Now that you mention it,
it's coming up soon.

35
00:02:33,160 --> 00:02:36,120
You're good at running festivals, Ryo-san.

36
00:02:36,120 --> 00:02:39,060
Could you take the trouble off my hands?

37
00:02:39,660 --> 00:02:41,060
Is that all?

38
00:02:42,700 --> 00:02:44,840
I'll put on a festival
that'll make everyone happy.

39
00:02:44,840 --> 00:02:46,080
Thank goodness.

40
00:02:46,700 --> 00:02:50,340
The truth is, only half the festival
donations have been collected so far.

41
00:02:50,340 --> 00:02:51,780
Half?

42
00:02:51,780 --> 00:02:53,780
Please, Ryo-san, I'm begging you.

43
00:02:53,780 --> 00:02:58,680
Only you can handle this crisis.
Not even Dr. Kametani could manage it.

44
00:03:02,080 --> 00:03:03,800
So I'll help out too.

45
00:03:03,800 --> 00:03:08,000
A perfect job for a
band-aid-fix guy like you, right?

46
00:03:08,760 --> 00:03:10,220
First things first.

47
00:03:11,940 --> 00:03:12,680
Excuse me.

48
00:03:12,680 --> 00:03:13,720
Welcome!

49
00:03:13,720 --> 00:03:16,140
Where's the old lady today?

50
00:03:16,140 --> 00:03:18,240
She went out with the old
ladies from the neighborhood

51
00:03:18,240 --> 00:03:20,380
to pray at Togenuki Jizo.

52
00:03:20,900 --> 00:03:21,340
I see.

53
00:03:21,340 --> 00:03:23,780
So it's the grannies' Harajuku

54
00:03:23,780 --> 00:03:25,960
Donations for the festival?

55
00:03:25,960 --> 00:03:26,820
Yes, please.

56
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:29,300
Well then, thanks.

57
00:03:29,300 --> 00:03:31,160
Thank you for your cooperation.

58
00:03:32,680 --> 00:03:33,680
Thank you very much.

59
00:03:34,620 --> 00:03:36,480
Thanks for your cooperation.

60
00:03:36,920 --> 00:03:37,680
Mm.

61
00:03:37,680 --> 00:03:39,615
Ten houses and only 10,000 yen.

62
00:03:39,665 --> 00:03:42,360
Doing this won't get us anywhere.

63
00:03:45,800 --> 00:03:48,840
Alright, if it's come to this,
we'll start with the wealthy places.

64
00:03:49,220 --> 00:03:51,282
Wait, wait, hold on, hold on,

65
00:03:51,332 --> 00:03:53,320
Ryo-san, what do you plan to do?

66
00:03:53,680 --> 00:03:55,480
The branch manager?

67
00:03:55,940 --> 00:03:59,220
Yes, tell him that Neighborhood
Chairman Ōkō has come.

68
00:03:59,500 --> 00:04:00,080
Y-yes.

69
00:04:00,420 --> 00:04:02,240
There are people waiting behind us,
so hurry up.

70
00:04:02,500 --> 00:04:03,140
Ryo-san.

71
00:04:06,600 --> 00:04:09,160
I'm the branch manager. Is there a problem?

72
00:04:09,160 --> 00:04:11,620
I came to ask for a
donation for the festival.

73
00:04:11,620 --> 00:04:14,040
A token amount is fine.

74
00:04:15,080 --> 00:04:15,980
A donation?

75
00:04:16,720 --> 00:04:17,720
Then here you go.

76
00:04:19,680 --> 00:04:20,680
What's this?

77
00:04:20,680 --> 00:04:22,800
What do you mean, what is it?
It's a donation.

78
00:04:22,800 --> 00:04:24,440
Just ten thousand yen?

79
00:04:24,440 --> 00:04:27,080
Everyone, listen up!

80
00:04:28,040 --> 00:04:31,660
A big bank like this only
gives ten thousand yen?

81
00:04:33,140 --> 00:04:34,280
Sorry, it's twenty thousand yen.

82
00:04:34,800 --> 00:04:35,640
Hold on a second!

83
00:04:38,740 --> 00:04:42,200
The festival is a great chance
to connect with local residents,

84
00:04:42,200 --> 00:04:46,720
or does what's written on this
poster not reflect your true feelings?

85
00:04:46,920 --> 00:04:49,460
Of course it does! It's our bank's motto.

86
00:04:49,460 --> 00:04:51,600
Ha then how about 50,000 yen

87
00:04:51,600 --> 00:04:52,620
given little by little!

88
00:04:53,200 --> 00:04:55,240
A whopping one million yen!

89
00:04:55,480 --> 00:04:58,740
Whoa, one million!? That's unreasonable.

90
00:04:58,740 --> 00:05:01,140
A budget of one million? No way!

91
00:05:03,140 --> 00:05:04,920
Do you have an account at this bank?

92
00:05:04,920 --> 00:05:06,320
I do, but

93
00:05:06,320 --> 00:05:08,560
starting today,
let's switch to another bank.

94
00:05:08,560 --> 00:05:09,160
Sounds good.

95
00:05:10,060 --> 00:05:10,540
That's...

96
00:05:11,840 --> 00:05:15,060
Everyone, stop banking with a
place that doesn't understand reason,

97
00:05:15,060 --> 00:05:17,860
and move your accounts
to the bank next door.

98
00:05:21,360 --> 00:05:23,880
I'll give it, I'll pay it, one million yen.

99
00:05:23,880 --> 00:05:26,040
You're not really overextending yourself,
are you?

100
00:05:26,040 --> 00:05:29,380
Donations are simply a way of expressing
gratitude to the local people.

101
00:05:29,380 --> 00:05:31,420
That's what they're meant to be, after all.

102
00:05:33,400 --> 00:05:33,920
Please.

103
00:05:33,920 --> 00:05:35,840
That's more like it.

104
00:05:38,140 --> 00:05:40,820
Zakuro Bank donates five million yen!

105
00:05:41,520 --> 00:05:47,120
Ryo-san, it's not just five million,

106
00:05:48,560 --> 00:05:50,840
it was great how it was settled so easily.

107
00:05:50,840 --> 00:05:53,000
A bank exists thanks to all of you.

108
00:05:53,000 --> 00:05:54,900
Saying they'd gladly contribute,

109
00:05:54,900 --> 00:05:56,760
even shedding tears.

110
00:05:58,420 --> 00:06:00,900
Of course,
his popularity is through the roof too.

111
00:06:00,900 --> 00:06:06,040
Everywhere you go, people want to
move their accounts to Zakuro Bank.

112
00:06:07,520 --> 00:06:08,980
So, what will you do?

113
00:06:08,980 --> 00:06:11,700
We'll contribute too.

114
00:06:14,420 --> 00:06:16,820
Five million yen, locked in!

115
00:06:16,820 --> 00:06:18,600
A promotion is guaranteed.

116
00:06:23,060 --> 00:06:25,360
Ryotsu's collecting donations like crazy.

117
00:06:25,360 --> 00:06:28,560
Apparently he's raised seven
million yen for the festival!

118
00:06:29,080 --> 00:06:32,500
I was forced into the neighborhood
association by my senior,

119
00:06:32,500 --> 00:06:33,960
and they charged me five
hundred thousand yen.

120
00:06:33,960 --> 00:06:35,120
Five hundred thousand yen?

121
00:06:35,580 --> 00:06:39,700
Apparently I'm a gold member of the Kameari neighborhood association,
or so I hear.

122
00:06:40,240 --> 00:06:41,400
That's ridiculous.

123
00:06:41,880 --> 00:06:45,020
They say they're even making the
mikoshi a luxurious special edition.

124
00:06:45,340 --> 00:06:48,300
What on earth is that guy thinking?

125
00:06:52,860 --> 00:06:53,960
So many people!

126
00:06:54,440 --> 00:06:56,680
The food stalls are all
sparkling and gaudy too.

127
00:06:56,680 --> 00:06:59,140
He just wants to make as much
noise and show as possible.

128
00:06:59,140 --> 00:07:01,440
That's the senior officer's personality on full display,
isn't it.

129
00:07:02,480 --> 00:07:04,180
The mikoshi has come out!

130
00:07:04,740 --> 00:07:07,960
Bush! Bush! Bush!

131
00:07:08,000 --> 00:07:09,120
Bush! Bush! Bush!

132
00:07:09,120 --> 00:07:11,340
Come on, bush! Bush! Bush!

133
00:07:13,020 --> 00:07:15,020
It's the Egg Festival!

134
00:07:15,980 --> 00:07:19,420
That guy with the four...
he's like a fish in water.

135
00:07:19,420 --> 00:07:21,960
He's been a festival lover since he was young,
hasn't he.

136
00:07:21,960 --> 00:07:24,580
Alright, go, fighting mikoshi!

137
00:07:32,900 --> 00:07:35,380
But festivals really are great, aren't they.

138
00:07:35,380 --> 00:07:38,260
The more people there are,
the more fun it feels, doesn't it.

139
00:07:38,940 --> 00:07:40,300
Yeah, well.

140
00:07:41,240 --> 00:07:42,020
Cheers!

141
00:07:42,020 --> 00:07:42,500
Coming!

142
00:07:44,400 --> 00:07:46,620
Thanks, Ryo-san, it's a huge success!

143
00:07:46,620 --> 00:07:47,960
Just like you, Ryo-san.

144
00:07:47,960 --> 00:07:52,840
If the crowds keep gathering like this,
the shopping district will be grateful too.

145
00:07:52,840 --> 00:07:56,740
Could you think of something else
that could help revitalize the town?

146
00:07:57,400 --> 00:07:58,500
Revitalize the town

147
00:07:58,500 --> 00:08:03,440
Yeah, I'll plan festival after festival,
one after another.

148
00:08:03,900 --> 00:08:06,580
Sounds great, festival after festival!

149
00:08:06,580 --> 00:08:09,960
Festivals all year round,
that'll be the talk of the town.

150
00:08:09,960 --> 00:08:12,760
Right, but first things first,
we'll need the money.

151
00:08:12,760 --> 00:08:16,460
Oh no, another festival?

152
00:08:16,460 --> 00:08:18,900
The last one was a windfall festival.

153
00:08:18,900 --> 00:08:21,680
The next one's the Kameari
Sleepy-Head Festival!

154
00:08:21,680 --> 00:08:24,780
But we just spent money on the last one!

155
00:08:24,780 --> 00:08:26,720
From now on, it's a festival every week!

156
00:08:26,720 --> 00:08:29,020
Next week is the Dontaku Festival.

157
00:08:29,020 --> 00:08:30,500
Then comes the Samba Carnival.

158
00:08:30,500 --> 00:08:31,800
Next up is the Naked Men's Festival.

159
00:08:31,800 --> 00:08:35,100
This holiday weekend is the
Special Thanks Wasshoi Festival!

160
00:08:35,580 --> 00:08:36,560
E-every week...

161
00:08:38,640 --> 00:08:41,840
Even so, with a festival every week, there's
a limit to how much we can ask for in donations.

162
00:08:42,300 --> 00:08:46,960
But 300 yen a month in neighborhood
dues won't add up to anything.

163
00:08:47,740 --> 00:08:49,120
Right, let's collect a tax.

164
00:08:49,780 --> 00:08:50,440
A tax?

165
00:08:50,620 --> 00:08:52,100
Are you serious, senior?

166
00:08:52,100 --> 00:08:53,440
Completely serious.

167
00:08:53,440 --> 00:08:55,820
There's national tax and
there's metropolitan tax, so

168
00:08:55,820 --> 00:08:58,160
why not have a neighborhood
association tax too?

169
00:08:58,800 --> 00:09:01,500
Some people take neighborhood dues
lightly and refuse to pay them.

170
00:09:01,500 --> 00:09:03,140
We'll make them pay it as a tax.

171
00:09:03,140 --> 00:09:06,020
But we can't just raise the dues, you know.

172
00:09:06,560 --> 00:09:07,540
I've thought of that too.

173
00:09:08,100 --> 00:09:10,220
How do we set up a
neighborhood-specific tax...

174
00:09:10,960 --> 00:09:12,840
It applies to absolutely everything.

175
00:09:12,840 --> 00:09:14,920
But will everyone pay it without complaint?

176
00:09:15,640 --> 00:09:18,760
So we'll switch the currency
from yen to hectopascals.

177
00:09:18,760 --> 00:09:23,180
100 hectopascals is
112.5 yen for 10,000 tons.

178
00:09:23,180 --> 00:09:24,940
That makes it feel cheap.

179
00:09:24,940 --> 00:09:28,840
The math is a hassle,
so everyone gets confused and pays.

180
00:09:28,840 --> 00:09:30,680
How sly!

181
00:09:31,200 --> 00:09:33,580
First, the detached
homes in the neighborhood.

182
00:09:33,580 --> 00:09:36,860
A flat annual tax of 1,000 hectopascals.

183
00:09:36,860 --> 00:09:41,120
Let's see, 100 hectopascals is 112.5 yen, so

184
00:09:41,120 --> 00:09:43,780
that comes to 1,125 yen.

185
00:09:43,780 --> 00:09:44,980
Isn't that a bit expensive?

186
00:09:44,980 --> 00:09:48,180
Condominiums for sale are
also 1,000 hectopascals.

187
00:09:48,180 --> 00:09:50,880
And if you keep pets,
there's a pet tax on top.

188
00:09:50,880 --> 00:09:52,400
Pedigreed pets are 500.

189
00:09:52,860 --> 00:09:54,240
Magazines are just 100.

190
00:09:54,820 --> 00:09:56,580
See? Doesn't it seem cheap?

191
00:09:56,580 --> 00:09:59,040
We'll collect from the kids too.

192
00:09:59,040 --> 00:10:01,960
A game recreation tax of 100 hectopascals.

193
00:10:03,580 --> 00:10:05,040
Collect from buses too.

194
00:10:05,040 --> 00:10:06,620
You're a tax demon, aren't you?

195
00:10:06,620 --> 00:10:09,180
This still isn't tough enough.

196
00:10:10,120 --> 00:10:10,620
That's it!

197
00:10:11,120 --> 00:10:13,620
Nakagawa,
you're in the Handsome Man Tax bracket.

198
00:10:13,620 --> 00:10:16,980
Maximum tax: 3,000 hectopascals.

199
00:10:16,980 --> 00:10:18,240
Handsome Man Tax?

200
00:10:18,400 --> 00:10:21,640
Handsome men already get
plenty of perks in this world,

201
00:10:21,640 --> 00:10:24,320
so they should have to pay plenty of tax.

202
00:10:24,320 --> 00:10:25,300
I-I see...

203
00:10:26,580 --> 00:10:31,000
Plus, anyone over 180 centimeters
tall pays the model physique tax.

204
00:10:31,000 --> 00:10:33,540
On top of that, playboy types get added on,

205
00:10:33,540 --> 00:10:36,060
9,800 hectopascals.

206
00:10:36,060 --> 00:10:37,420
That's absurd!

207
00:10:37,900 --> 00:10:38,500
Reiko.

208
00:10:38,500 --> 00:10:40,920
Reiko, as a beauty, pays 3,000.

209
00:10:40,920 --> 00:10:43,320
Plus, the model physique group,

210
00:10:43,320 --> 00:10:44,360
the busty group,

211
00:10:44,360 --> 00:10:45,160
the seductive group,

212
00:10:45,160 --> 00:10:46,260
the alluring group,

213
00:10:46,260 --> 00:10:48,780
"Oh, I can't resist!" and so on.

214
00:10:48,780 --> 00:10:50,920
That comes to a total
of 20,000 hectopascals.

215
00:10:50,920 --> 00:10:52,340
You've got to be joking.

216
00:10:52,820 --> 00:10:55,220
I don't even live in this neighborhood.

217
00:10:55,220 --> 00:10:57,860
The moment you set foot
in this neighborhood,

218
00:10:57,860 --> 00:10:59,540
you have to follow this law.

219
00:11:01,000 --> 00:11:03,320
So I have to pay too

220
00:11:04,260 --> 00:11:06,720
You're exempt.
You fall under the basic deduction.

221
00:11:06,720 --> 00:11:10,840
Really? I think it'd be
around 10 hectopascals, though.

222
00:11:11,880 --> 00:11:14,220
What on earth is all the commotion about?

223
00:11:14,760 --> 00:11:15,880
Chief.

224
00:11:15,880 --> 00:11:18,820
Congratulations, Chief!

225
00:11:19,520 --> 00:11:20,620
What's all this, all of a sudden?

226
00:11:20,620 --> 00:11:24,540
In your case,
it's so outrageous you'll get a tax refund!

227
00:11:24,540 --> 00:11:26,680
A refund? So the tax gets returned?

228
00:11:26,680 --> 00:11:28,780
Well, that's a relief.

229
00:11:29,220 --> 00:11:31,820
That's 2,000 hectopascals a year.

230
00:11:32,680 --> 00:11:35,900
Alright, let's collect taxes left and right!

231
00:11:36,740 --> 00:11:39,400
You two are awfully devoted to standing and reading,
aren't you?

232
00:11:39,840 --> 00:11:43,040
Yes, the standing-and-reading
tax is 95 hectopascals.

233
00:11:43,040 --> 00:11:46,180
Standing-and-reading tax?
Is that even allowed?

234
00:11:46,320 --> 00:11:49,840
It's for making the foot Kameyari,
so hand it over quickly.

235
00:11:50,440 --> 00:11:52,520
You two are working hard, aren't you?

236
00:11:53,040 --> 00:11:56,520
Crap-split tax, 68 hectopascals.
Thank you very much.

237
00:11:57,080 --> 00:11:57,760
What did you just say?

238
00:11:58,780 --> 00:11:59,140
Take that!

239
00:12:01,080 --> 00:12:05,100
Yes, the mobile phone tax for what
you were just using is 111 hectopascals.

240
00:12:05,920 --> 00:12:07,240
Don't fuck around with me!

241
00:12:08,080 --> 00:12:11,280
That was a back-talk tax,
plus a spitting tax!

242
00:12:11,660 --> 00:12:12,980
Pay up, quick!

243
00:12:12,980 --> 00:12:13,880
Y-yes...

244
00:12:15,460 --> 00:12:18,860
Staff, from here on we're
collecting the entry tax.

245
00:12:18,860 --> 00:12:21,000
Well, our place is right over there,
you know.

246
00:12:21,000 --> 00:12:23,300
This is the checkpoint,
so it can't be helped, right?

247
00:12:23,740 --> 00:12:26,500
If you're bringing a dog,
we'll also charge the pet tax.

248
00:12:27,220 --> 00:12:30,560
With this much,
that's enough for the next Nemuke Festival.

249
00:12:31,500 --> 00:12:34,940
It's still not enough for building the
new neighborhood association building.

250
00:12:34,940 --> 00:12:39,060
A new neighborhood association building? Weren't we
doing this to revitalize the town through the festival?

251
00:12:39,540 --> 00:12:41,640
It's already the 21st century.

252
00:12:42,000 --> 00:12:44,720
In a tenement like something
out of a rakugo story,

253
00:12:44,720 --> 00:12:47,120
can we build a 21st-century town?

254
00:12:47,120 --> 00:12:51,340
The 21st century needs a container befitting the 21st century,
doesn't it?

255
00:12:51,340 --> 00:12:53,240
That's the new neighborhood
association building.

256
00:12:53,240 --> 00:12:54,660
The festival comes after that.

257
00:12:55,100 --> 00:12:56,160
Is that so?

258
00:12:56,500 --> 00:12:56,660
Mm.

259
00:12:58,420 --> 00:13:00,420
Collect taxes galore!

260
00:13:00,420 --> 00:13:11,940
Still, it feels good to have a place where you can look down on people.
We'll decide the construction at this eye level. Yosh!

261
00:13:12,400 --> 00:13:12,580
Hey.

262
00:13:14,980 --> 00:13:21,100
Do you really think you can build something like this with taxpayers' money?
Who do you think you're talking to, Chief?

263
00:13:21,460 --> 00:13:25,220
I'm the temporary neighborhood association chief,
entrusted with full authority.

264
00:13:25,220 --> 00:13:28,060
I'd appreciate it if you
didn't interfere with what I do.

265
00:13:28,060 --> 00:13:30,620
But isn't this going a bit too far?

266
00:13:31,020 --> 00:13:33,100
We're going to change Japan,
starting from Kameari.

267
00:13:33,100 --> 00:13:34,000
Senpai.

268
00:13:34,000 --> 00:13:34,660
Ryo-chan.

269
00:13:34,660 --> 00:13:35,460
Ryo-san.

270
00:13:35,460 --> 00:13:37,780
Building that office was a mistake.

271
00:13:37,780 --> 00:13:39,920
The complaint calls won't stop ringing.

272
00:13:39,920 --> 00:13:43,440
Taxes are so high that people
keep leaving the neighborhood.

273
00:13:43,440 --> 00:13:48,120
The shopping district is completely
empty and turning into a ghost town.

274
00:13:48,120 --> 00:13:50,960
The hectopascal currency has crashed.

275
00:13:51,100 --> 00:13:53,060
What? Look at the sky!

276
00:13:56,480 --> 00:13:58,500
What ghost town? Don't be ridiculous.

277
00:13:58,500 --> 00:14:00,480
Look, there are so many people!

278
00:14:00,480 --> 00:14:06,540
Those are people who are
fond of it a thousandfold.

279
00:14:06,540 --> 00:14:07,360
W-what?

280
00:14:09,420 --> 00:14:12,280
Well then, that's enough play for now.

281
00:14:12,280 --> 00:14:15,500
I'm handing things over to the
veteran neighborhood association chief.

282
00:14:15,500 --> 00:14:16,720
That's not fair.

283
00:14:17,620 --> 00:14:18,460
Why?

284
00:14:25,620 --> 00:14:26,780
Leave the rest to you.

285
00:14:41,420 --> 00:14:43,640
I heard Chōkai-chō got hurt,

286
00:14:43,640 --> 00:14:45,040
yeah, that's right.

287
00:14:45,040 --> 00:14:48,440
He slipped off a ladder while fixing the roof,
apparently.

288
00:14:48,440 --> 00:14:50,320
That's what you get for doing
something you're not used to.

289
00:14:52,940 --> 00:14:54,320
Well then, I guess I'll go with that.

290
00:14:56,800 --> 00:14:57,660
Excuse me.

291
00:14:57,660 --> 00:14:58,780
It's Ryo-san.

292
00:14:58,780 --> 00:15:01,380
I heard you got hurt, so I'm coming in.

293
00:15:01,920 --> 00:15:03,340
How are you feeling?

294
00:15:03,340 --> 00:15:05,960
Ugh, here for the disciplinary
tax collection again?

295
00:15:07,060 --> 00:15:09,700
No, that was abolished, wasn't it?

296
00:15:10,220 --> 00:15:13,360
It's just a visit.
Apparently he fell off a ladder.

297
00:15:14,360 --> 00:15:15,442
I see,

298
00:15:15,492 --> 00:15:18,700
I was thinking about neighborhood association stuff,
and it just popped into my head,

299
00:15:18,700 --> 00:15:19,840
you know.

300
00:15:19,840 --> 00:15:22,920
What about the neighborhood association?

301
00:15:23,260 --> 00:15:26,360
I want to give this neighborhood
some unique character of its own.

302
00:15:26,720 --> 00:15:31,080
A town where UFOs land, a town of dinosaurs,
a town where stone tools get dug up,

303
00:15:31,080 --> 00:15:36,680
I see. So you want to draw people in and stir up the town,
is that it?

304
00:15:36,680 --> 00:15:38,240
Alright, leave it to me.

305
00:15:38,240 --> 00:15:40,180
W-wait a minute, Ryo-san.

306
00:15:40,180 --> 00:15:43,460
After last time's tax mess, we can't go
through that kind of pushy fight again.

307
00:15:44,160 --> 00:15:48,440
Easier said than done.
Isn't there some clever way to do this?

308
00:15:49,840 --> 00:15:51,920
Still, it's a town full of old men.

309
00:15:51,920 --> 00:15:53,560
Where are the old ladies?

310
00:15:54,280 --> 00:15:56,100
The neighborhood grannies

311
00:15:56,100 --> 00:15:58,140
are all off to pray at Togenuki Jizō.

312
00:15:58,680 --> 00:16:01,280
The grandmas' Harajuku

313
00:16:02,280 --> 00:16:03,980
Harajuku is for the young ones,

314
00:16:03,980 --> 00:16:06,380
and Togenuki Jizō is for the grannies.

315
00:16:06,380 --> 00:16:08,160
So the old men get nothing?

316
00:16:08,160 --> 00:16:10,120
Ryo-san, wait!

317
00:16:10,120 --> 00:16:12,780
It's not like last time,
when we left everything to you.

318
00:16:12,780 --> 00:16:13,160
That's right.

319
00:16:13,520 --> 00:16:15,680
We're going to make Kameari
the old men's Harajuku.

320
00:16:16,500 --> 00:16:17,900
Leave it to me.

321
00:16:25,480 --> 00:16:28,320
Yo-sa, what are you cooking up this time?

322
00:16:28,320 --> 00:16:31,720
Just watch me.

323
00:16:31,720 --> 00:16:32,420
What?

324
00:16:32,420 --> 00:16:34,280
Grandpa's Harajuku.

325
00:16:35,000 --> 00:16:38,560
The ones with money now and
nowhere to spend it are the old men.

326
00:16:39,100 --> 00:16:41,740
I'll gather grandpas from all
over the country right here.

327
00:16:41,740 --> 00:16:42,920
But how, exactly?

328
00:16:43,700 --> 00:16:44,880
Take the public bathhouse, for example.

329
00:16:45,460 --> 00:16:48,100
The tiles are all go and shogi boards.

330
00:16:49,840 --> 00:16:50,380
Dim, like the Pure Land.

331
00:16:50,840 --> 00:16:53,660
At the community hall,
a karaoke class for seniors.

332
00:16:54,300 --> 00:16:57,240
At the station square,
a world destruction history expo.

333
00:16:57,820 --> 00:17:00,700
Blood pressure checks available
anywhere along the shopping street.

334
00:17:00,700 --> 00:17:03,680
Homemade diabetes diet classes held.

335
00:17:03,680 --> 00:17:06,800
And in the park,
a hero of the old men's association.

336
00:17:06,800 --> 00:17:08,380
A statue of Mito Kōmon.

337
00:17:09,040 --> 00:17:10,460
With all this in place,

338
00:17:10,460 --> 00:17:14,020
there's no doubt the old
men will flock here in droves.

339
00:17:21,480 --> 00:17:22,320
Why?

340
00:17:22,320 --> 00:17:25,240
Why hasn't a single old man come?

341
00:17:25,240 --> 00:17:27,040
I have no idea.

342
00:17:27,040 --> 00:17:29,220
The image of old men Ryo-chan has in mind

343
00:17:29,220 --> 00:17:32,200
must be too far from real old men, isn't it?

344
00:17:33,340 --> 00:17:36,580
Isn't asking the elderly
about the elderly the best way?

345
00:17:38,420 --> 00:17:40,140
Acquaintances of the elderly

346
00:17:43,920 --> 00:17:45,680
I just pictured an unpleasant face.

347
00:17:51,920 --> 00:17:53,480
Why the gloomy face?

348
00:17:53,480 --> 00:17:55,240
The real deal?

349
00:17:56,640 --> 00:17:58,680
Ryo-chan's grandpa.

350
00:17:59,040 --> 00:18:00,280
Ryotsu Kanbei, that's me.

351
00:18:00,680 --> 00:18:02,340
I'm a doting grandpa, you know.

352
00:18:02,340 --> 00:18:03,320
Perfect timing.

353
00:18:03,320 --> 00:18:05,360
Why don't you consult your grandfather?

354
00:18:05,740 --> 00:18:06,940
That's right, Ryo-chan.

355
00:18:06,940 --> 00:18:09,220
They say age beats the shell, after all.

356
00:18:13,820 --> 00:18:15,440
Will this really work?

357
00:18:15,640 --> 00:18:19,320
It'll be a failure, Israel.
It's for my cute grandchildren.

358
00:18:19,540 --> 00:18:21,540
I'm worried about that lightness of yours.

359
00:18:21,740 --> 00:18:24,320
I didn't live to 104 for nothing.

360
00:18:24,660 --> 00:18:28,140
We've built in the know-how
to meet the needs of old men.

361
00:18:30,380 --> 00:18:34,060
The average age of our employees is 88.

362
00:18:34,160 --> 00:18:34,540
What?

363
00:18:34,700 --> 00:18:37,250
He's the designer of
the cute girl characters.

364
00:18:37,300 --> 00:18:38,860
Adachi-kun, age 92.

365
00:18:39,000 --> 00:18:41,380
He also worked at Mr.
Shigeru Sugiura's studio.

366
00:18:42,040 --> 00:18:44,200
The gap with the characters is incredible.

367
00:18:44,200 --> 00:18:49,420
He's the mecha designer for robots,
Hattori, age 87.

368
00:18:49,420 --> 00:18:52,540
The robots are very modern too.

369
00:18:52,540 --> 00:18:56,320
On top of that, we're developing
a fighting game just for old men.

370
00:18:56,320 --> 00:18:59,660
A fighting game?
Do old men actually play fighting games?

371
00:19:00,100 --> 00:19:03,300
Even old men can become
superhumans in the game.

372
00:19:03,300 --> 00:19:06,940
The thrill of beating up
young punks on your behalf...

373
00:19:06,940 --> 00:19:09,700
There's something no
one can replace it with.

374
00:19:11,380 --> 00:19:20,220
Think about it. Do you see why it failed? It means the
idea that it was because they were old men was wrong.

375
00:19:21,680 --> 00:19:24,780
From now on,
the keyword for old men is game consoles.

376
00:19:25,440 --> 00:19:30,120
Nice! It didn't catch on.

377
00:19:30,120 --> 00:19:35,240
I was just seeing old
men in a superficial way.

378
00:19:35,240 --> 00:19:36,195
Exactly.

379
00:19:36,245 --> 00:19:39,260
Leave everything to me.

380
00:19:39,980 --> 00:19:41,426
First, the public bath:

381
00:19:41,476 --> 00:19:44,220
put a young, beautiful woman at the counter,

382
00:19:44,220 --> 00:19:48,160
and instead of walls,
show a water-themed program on a large TV.

383
00:19:48,160 --> 00:19:52,640
At the community center,
a concert by a cover band of old men.

384
00:19:52,640 --> 00:19:55,920
In the station plaza,
a Parapara dance class.

385
00:19:55,920 --> 00:19:58,700
In the shopping street, Silver Purikura.

386
00:20:00,120 --> 00:20:02,240
You can even take two-shots
with the Beitore Hit!

387
00:20:02,640 --> 00:20:05,260
And a game center just for old men!

388
00:20:05,280 --> 00:20:06,760
A hangout for old ladies!

389
00:20:06,960 --> 00:20:10,940
At the movie theater, a sci-fi
blockbuster you can only see in Kameari:

390
00:20:10,940 --> 00:20:13,720
Screening Hypertension Ojin-gelion!

391
00:20:13,960 --> 00:20:15,840
Damn it! Show us some youth!

392
00:20:16,000 --> 00:20:16,400
Yes!

393
00:20:16,940 --> 00:20:19,520
Hypertension Game Center!

394
00:20:21,560 --> 00:20:23,940
Next casualty, from Ojin-gelion!

395
00:20:25,660 --> 00:20:28,480
We'll also open a convenience
store just for old men!

396
00:20:30,120 --> 00:20:34,500
With all this in place, there's no
doubt old men will move in and flock here.

397
00:20:38,020 --> 00:20:39,740
Wow, what a crowd!

398
00:20:40,200 --> 00:20:43,700
Look left, look right, it's all old men.

399
00:20:43,700 --> 00:20:46,980
The Kameari Grandpa Town
plan is a huge success.

400
00:20:47,840 --> 00:20:50,660
Ryo-san,
this time it really is a huge success!

401
00:20:50,660 --> 00:20:52,940
Sales are up 50%!

402
00:20:52,940 --> 00:20:55,860
Our shop's up 35%!

403
00:20:55,860 --> 00:20:57,640
Ours is shooting up too!

404
00:20:57,640 --> 00:21:01,900
Kamearé is now the talk
of grandpas all over Japan.

405
00:21:01,900 --> 00:21:05,180
The talk of grandpas all over Japan

406
00:21:05,180 --> 00:21:06,960
Good for you, senpai.

407
00:21:06,960 --> 00:21:09,180
Right, next up is this.

408
00:21:09,180 --> 00:21:10,740
Senpai...

409
00:21:11,680 --> 00:21:14,700
What, you're holding a
Woodstock for grandpas?

410
00:21:15,280 --> 00:21:20,480
That's right. This time we'll gather grandpas
from around the world in Kameari for a huge event.

411
00:21:20,480 --> 00:21:21,760
Now that's something.

412
00:21:21,760 --> 00:21:25,220
Use the internet to call out
to grandpas all over the world.

413
00:21:25,680 --> 00:21:26,420
Got it.

414
00:21:27,640 --> 00:21:30,929
Hurry, hurry!
Build an airport on this Arakawa riverbank,

415
00:21:30,979 --> 00:21:34,000
and fly grandpas in from all
over the world on direct flights!

416
00:21:35,340 --> 00:21:38,920
Ryotsu's at it again,
cooking up something new?

417
00:21:39,140 --> 00:21:42,080
Yes, apparently it's an
international airport just for old men.

418
00:21:42,560 --> 00:21:45,700
He's supposedly gathering old men
from all over the world to Kameari.

419
00:21:45,700 --> 00:21:48,517
And he's building a new hotel too,
apparently.

420
00:21:48,567 --> 00:21:50,180
An airport just for old men...

421
00:21:50,180 --> 00:21:54,120
Honestly, that idiot knows no limits.

422
00:21:58,340 --> 00:22:00,340
Let's all go to Kamerarii!

423
00:22:00,340 --> 00:22:03,240
That place is Kamerarii.

424
00:22:03,240 --> 00:22:04,680
Connected through melody.

425
00:22:04,680 --> 00:22:06,540
Artist Kamerarii!

426
00:22:06,540 --> 00:22:08,560
Artist Kōchū Kamerarii!

427
00:22:08,560 --> 00:22:09,740
Look at everyone.

428
00:22:09,740 --> 00:22:11,260
Our town.

429
00:22:11,800 --> 00:22:13,520
Let's become Kamerarii'd!

430
00:22:39,380 --> 00:22:41,820
Yay! It's a huge success!

431
00:22:51,080 --> 00:22:51,960
I'm exhausted!

432
00:22:53,080 --> 00:22:55,400
Wh-wait, did too many people gather?

433
00:22:55,720 --> 00:22:58,120
Ion-san! Do something!

434
00:22:58,420 --> 00:23:02,060
At this rate, the numbers will overflow
and the shopping street will be wrecked!

435
00:23:02,180 --> 00:23:04,340
But even so...

436
00:23:05,940 --> 00:23:06,800
Here they come again!

437
00:23:09,380 --> 00:23:12,040
It's all our fault, everyone's overjoyed!

438
00:23:12,700 --> 00:23:13,500
Don't run away!

439
00:23:17,980 --> 00:23:21,600
Then, leave the rest to the veteran
neighborhood association chief...

440
00:23:21,600 --> 00:23:22,900
That trick again!

441
00:23:28,080 --> 00:23:30,820
Whoa, we're being swallowed
by a wave of old men!

442
00:23:44,140 --> 00:23:46,200
Apparently Chōkai-chō is a
"fish from another world," they say.

443
00:23:46,700 --> 00:23:47,420
That's right.

444
00:23:47,420 --> 00:23:50,480
There's been so much going on to make my stomach hurt,
you know.

445
00:23:50,480 --> 00:23:53,440
Ryo-chan, anyway, when I went to visit...

446
00:23:53,440 --> 00:23:55,780
Yeah...

447
00:23:55,780 --> 00:23:57,560
Guess I'll do that, then.

448
00:23:59,240 --> 00:24:00,960
You don't need to come anymore.

449
00:24:15,160 --> 00:24:20,480
An afternoon after the rain,
as if someone is calling

450
00:24:21,800 --> 00:24:27,140
Walking and looking back,
pulled along by the clatter

451
00:24:28,300 --> 00:24:34,480
That strange feeling I had back then

452
00:24:34,480 --> 00:24:39,540
So, on the arcade street's tiles,

453
00:24:39,540 --> 00:24:45,340
I tried walking only on the black ones.

454
00:24:47,820 --> 00:24:51,500
Everyone was a child once,

455
00:24:51,500 --> 00:24:53,600
but everyone forgets.

456
00:24:54,520 --> 00:24:57,640
Politicians with their self-important faces

457
00:24:57,640 --> 00:25:00,940
and aunties with blue eyeshadow

458
00:25:00,940 --> 00:25:06,520
Go on, turn at that corner

459
00:25:07,500 --> 00:25:11,760
You'll get to meet everyone, everyone.

460
00:25:12,300 --> 00:25:19,660
Over there is Kameari
surely Kameari is there.

461
00:25:20,940 --> 00:25:24,960
Everyone, come on over to our town.

462
00:25:25,740 --> 00:25:26,480
Thank you.

463
00:25:29,440 --> 00:25:31,860
They say this is the machine
that measures TV ratings.

464
00:25:31,860 --> 00:25:33,360
Is that really true, Hojo?

465
00:25:33,360 --> 00:25:37,480
Wait, TV people should want even
one percent more in their numbers.

466
00:25:37,480 --> 00:25:40,760
If I could control
everything about this machine,

467
00:25:40,760 --> 00:25:43,820
I might even be able to become a god.

468
00:25:43,820 --> 00:25:47,580
See you next time,
the man who stole the ratings.

469
00:25:56,480 --> 00:25:59,260
Everyone, come on over to our town.

470
00:26:00,340 --> 00:26:00,860
Thank you.

